1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
ORBITAL explores the universe while asking the system to explain the data behind the view.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:17,000
A comparison exposes the flaw: the dates are wrong, but matching sample counts still pass.

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Data validation and investigation design improve. An unevaluated skill is unloaded, not counted as a success.

4
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:42,000
The new connector rejects shifted dates and is later reused to retrieve Mars data.

5
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:49,000
The product evolves too: early Saturn rings resemble evenly spaced discs.

6
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:56,000
Finer ring bands and a corrected plane follow. This is a product revision, not a single-variable experiment.

7
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Actual interactions show the final observatory. Values, reference frames and display effects stay distinct.

8
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Two capability types are adopted and reused. The required skill remains incomplete.
